(4539635, 651165, 71376, '<td valign="top">this is the ONLY image i have ever submitted on which i have not received any negative feedback :) .. happy me lol....<br/>and for those who could not relate to the title, id have a brief -<br/>when we are young, we are extremely playful, our whole existence is a play, keys becomes toys, and every tiny thing just becomes so much more playful... but as we grow older, and we learn about life, we lose that playfulness in ourselves, keys do nothing more than open doors.. so the balloons are symbolic to our childhood pleasures and "handicap" as we are no longer capable of getting any joy from them... lol i hope this makes sense ;) ..<br/> <br/>thanks to everyone who voted!</td>', 'this is the ONLY image i have ever submitted on which i have not received any negative feedback :) .. happy me lol....and for those who could not relate to the title, id have a brief -when we are young, we are extremely playful, our whole existence is a play, keys becomes toys, and every tiny thing just becomes so much more playful... but as we grow older, and we learn about life, we lose that playfulness in ourselves, keys do nothing more than open doors.. so the balloons are symbolic to our childhood pleasures and "handicap" as we are no longer capable of getting any joy from them... lol i hope this makes sense ;) .. thanks to everyone who voted!', '2008-03-05 03:13:08.000000', NULL, 0),
