(4543175, 651735, 66597, '<td valign="top">Well Deb, this didn''t do too badly after all :-) I''ve already commented on the Critical Mass thread about this one, but reiterate that I really like the tilt you chose and just that tiny drop of red on the golf ball.</td>', 'Well Deb, this didn''t do too badly after all :-) I''ve already commented on the Critical Mass thread about this one, but reiterate that I really like the tilt you chose and just that tiny drop of red on the golf ball.', '2008-03-06 11:44:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543185, 649562, 66597, '<td valign="top">I like the idea here a lot, and the title is great, as is the curve presented by the dominoes. I suspect technical issues brought you down - the white balance looks a little off here - there''s a bit of a yellowish cast to the dominoes and a gray cast to background. There are also a few bits of dust/hair that you maybe could have cloned from the background, since this is advanced. Mainly, though, I think the shadows may have been problematic to some viewers (including myself). I did not think they were deliberately used to enhance the photo (though of course I could be wrong on this), but instead the result of uneven lighting (I''m guessing you used flash here). If you have a light tent, this would be an interesting study to try again, as you could eliminate the shadows. Anyway, just my .02, hope it is helpful!</td>', 'I like the idea here a lot, and the title is great, as is the curve presented by the dominoes. I suspect technical issues brought you down - the white balance looks a little off here - there''s a bit of a yellowish cast to the dominoes and a gray cast to background. There are also a few bits of dust/hair that you maybe could have cloned from the background, since this is advanced. Mainly, though, I think the shadows may have been problematic to some viewers (including myself). I did not think they were deliberately used to enhance the photo (though of course I could be wrong on this), but instead the result of uneven lighting (I''m guessing you used flash here). If you have a light tent, this would be an interesting study to try again, as you could eliminate the shadows. Anyway, just my .02, hope it is helpful!', '2008-03-06 11:49:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543192, 651807, 66597, '<td valign="top">This definitely fits the challenge very nicely, and is well-focused with overall nice lighting. Some things that maybe could have brought this a higher score - there are a lot of branches, and so it''s a little hard to focus on anything specifically. I''m especially distracted by the branches on the left side and small ones coming up from the bottom. I do think you have a very strong background with some nice variations in shades that give depth.</td>', 'This definitely fits the challenge very nicely, and is well-focused with overall nice lighting. Some things that maybe could have brought this a higher score - there are a lot of branches, and so it''s a little hard to focus on anything specifically. I''m especially distracted by the branches on the left side and small ones coming up from the bottom. I do think you have a very strong background with some nice variations in shades that give depth.', '2008-03-06 11:52:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543198, 651706, 66597, '<td valign="top">Terry, I think this is really beautiful. I was one of your 9''s. I''m a bit stumped by those who gave you 1''s, 2''s, 3''s and 4''s - what were they thinking? My only nit is the bush on the left-hand side - it pulls my eyes out of the photo a bit - I think it would be stronger with some clean space in that area. However, it''s a minor nit, and this is a very, very strong photo with a story to it. Great title, by the way.</td>', 'Terry, I think this is really beautiful. I was one of your 9''s. I''m a bit stumped by those who gave you 1''s, 2''s, 3''s and 4''s - what were they thinking? My only nit is the bush on the left-hand side - it pulls my eyes out of the photo a bit - I think it would be stronger with some clean space in that area. However, it''s a minor nit, and this is a very, very strong photo with a story to it. Great title, by the way.', '2008-03-06 11:54:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543203, 651962, 66597, '<td valign="top">Ah, Colleen, I recall voting on this and looking at it multiple times. I find it interesting and artistic, but find myself wishing for one thing - that the beautiful lines in the top left extended down further. I was one of your 7''s, by the way. It''s nice to see a truly creative take on this challenge.</td>', 'Ah, Colleen, I recall voting on this and looking at it multiple times. I find it interesting and artistic, but find myself wishing for one thing - that the beautiful lines in the top left extended down further. I was one of your 7''s, by the way. It''s nice to see a truly creative take on this challenge.', '2008-03-06 11:57:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543204, 650123, 66597, '<td valign="top">Jeb, this is a beautiful scene and I love the lines in the tree branches. I do think this would have more impact if the tree stood out a bit more from the background, but realize that may have been an artistic choice on your part.</td>', 'Jeb, this is a beautiful scene and I love the lines in the tree branches. I do think this would have more impact if the tree stood out a bit more from the background, but realize that may have been an artistic choice on your part.', '2008-03-06 11:58:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543207, 649660, 66597, '<td valign="top">I got a good chuckle when I voted on this photo. Looks perfect for a stock site - I think it would be a good seller. It''s well lit, well-focused, and has nice composition. I think the only reason you didn''t score higher is that there isn''t too much else to do to "jazz up" the subject, and we all know that DPC voters are always looking for that "wow" factor. It''s a great, very solid photo, though, and as I said, should do well as stock.</td>', 'I got a good chuckle when I voted on this photo. Looks perfect for a stock site - I think it would be a good seller. It''s well lit, well-focused, and has nice composition. I think the only reason you didn''t score higher is that there isn''t too much else to do to "jazz up" the subject, and we all know that DPC voters are always looking for that "wow" factor. It''s a great, very solid photo, though, and as I said, should do well as stock.', '2008-03-06 12:01:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543209, 652002, 66597, '<td valign="top">Ernie - I really like this a lot - I was one of your 7''s. I think the interplay of textures is very interesting and doubtlessly unappreciated by the voters. The only thing that kept me from an even higher vote is that I''d like to see a little more of the river and just a bit less gray in the snow. Nicely done!</td>', 'Ernie - I really like this a lot - I was one of your 7''s. I think the interplay of textures is very interesting and doubtlessly unappreciated by the voters. The only thing that kept me from an even higher vote is that I''d like to see a little more of the river and just a bit less gray in the snow. Nicely done!', '2008-03-06 12:03:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543212, 649288, 66597, '<td valign="top">To me, one of the most under-appreciated entries in this challenge. I was one of your 8''s. I love the simplicity, lighting, and slight shadow. Very nice work!</td>', 'To me, one of the most under-appreciated entries in this challenge. I was one of your 8''s. I love the simplicity, lighting, and slight shadow. Very nice work!', '2008-03-06 12:04:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543218, 650510, 66597, '<td valign="top">I find this a most interesting photo, and under-appreciated by the voters. I really like the sense of chaos, which could be a deliberate metaphor for the war. I think you should consider entering this in some different venues. It may not be the "right" kind of eye-candy shot for DPC, but has a lot of merit and is a photo of which you should be proud.</td>', 'I find this a most interesting photo, and under-appreciated by the voters. I really like the sense of chaos, which could be a deliberate metaphor for the war. I think you should consider entering this in some different venues. It may not be the "right" kind of eye-candy shot for DPC, but has a lot of merit and is a photo of which you should be proud.', '2008-03-06 12:06:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543301, 651404, 32997, '<td valign="top">beautiful work!</td>', 'beautiful work!', '2008-03-06 12:58:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543367, 652018, 88656, '<td valign="top">VERY cool! :D<br/></td>', 'VERY cool! :D', '2008-03-06 13:26:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543501, 651759, 30982, '<td valign="top">This worked for me.</td>', 'This worked for me.', '2008-03-06 14:24:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543503, 651759, 62318, '<td valign="top">Funny juxtapostion of the pieces and the players themselves. Good stuff. Though maybe a slightly higher or lower angle just for added effect. Still ingenious entry. Bummer on the score.</td>', 'Funny juxtapostion of the pieces and the players themselves. Good stuff. Though maybe a slightly higher or lower angle just for added effect. Still ingenious entry. Bummer on the score.', '2008-03-06 14:25:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543507, 651979, 30982, '<td valign="top">And here I thought a signature was something akin to a flock, but with only four.  I''m in awe of the fact you can see snow across the body of the birds.  Were you driving along beside them or stopped?  Not that it matters - I''m just curious.  And I agree with Colleen.  Print on canvas, large, then hang.</td>', 'And here I thought a signature was something akin to a flock, but with only four.  I''m in awe of the fact you can see snow across the body of the birds.  Were you driving along beside them or stopped?  Not that it matters - I''m just curious.  And I agree with Colleen.  Print on canvas, large, then hang.', '2008-03-06 14:27:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543510, 650610, 62318, '<td valign="top">I like the striking color contrast. Good use of the frame and a terrific natural reference. Something that everyone knows but does not necessarily see.</td>', 'I like the striking color contrast. Good use of the frame and a terrific natural reference. Something that everyone knows but does not necessarily see.', '2008-03-06 14:28:49.000000', NULL, 0),
