(4550857, 651090, 67697, '<td valign="top">I like this better than the outtake.  I think this would have looked pretty cool in the leading lines challenge too.  This reminds me of that joke "What''s black and white, and read all over" lol.  (A kid''s joke if you do not know what I am talking about).  It''s a great find.  Should have scored higher.</td>', 'I like this better than the outtake.  I think this would have looked pretty cool in the leading lines challenge too.  This reminds me of that joke "What''s black and white, and read all over" lol.  (A kid''s joke if you do not know what I am talking about).  It''s a great find.  Should have scored higher.', '2008-03-09 21:58:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4550889, 652056, 67697, '<td valign="top">Hmmm doing quite well now I see since you stole the brown ribbon from me :P   This is very good.  I love the lighting and the reflections.  Beautiful detail on the egg shells as well.  Congrats on the 6+ score!</td>', 'Hmmm doing quite well now I see since you stole the brown ribbon from me :P   This is very good.  I love the lighting and the reflections.  Beautiful detail on the egg shells as well.  Congrats on the 6+ score!', '2008-03-09 22:07:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4550924, 650510, 67697, '<td valign="top">Charlene this is a really cool capture.  I love the bluish, ghostly tones of the etchings.  Actually, the brownish reflections look kind of ghostly as well.  Excellent perspective.</td>', 'Charlene this is a really cool capture.  I love the bluish, ghostly tones of the etchings.  Actually, the brownish reflections look kind of ghostly as well.  Excellent perspective.', '2008-03-09 22:18:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4550948, 650156, 67697, '<td valign="top">Um, where to go with my comments here lol.  Not sure if you were doing some kind of freudian study here but I have to say that my first thoughts (after seeing the photo and reading the title) closely matched those of <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=90658" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tootsweet</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=88204" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">choltmeier</a>.  Maybe it''s me, but now I will never look that this memorial the same again.  I will be chuckling of course because, well, this is pretty damn funny.<br/> <br/>Aside from that, more great use of lighting and the details are all so fluid and smooth.  :)</td>', 'Um, where to go with my comments here lol.  Not sure if you were doing some kind of freudian study here but I have to say that my first thoughts (after seeing the photo and reading the title) closely matched those of  tootsweet and  choltmeier.  Maybe it''s me, but now I will never look that this memorial the same again.  I will be chuckling of course because, well, this is pretty damn funny. Aside from that, more great use of lighting and the details are all so fluid and smooth.  :)', '2008-03-09 22:30:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551286, 649922, 31637, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful pattern and such great tonal ranges.</td>', 'What a beautiful pattern and such great tonal ranges.', '2008-03-10 01:24:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551454, 650391, 57229, '<td valign="top">Too damned clever by half. More than half, judging by the voters'' reactions.<br/>An OOBIE nomination is a little oddball feather in your cap, even if your name isn''t pulled out of the envelope. You get my vote.<br/>Damn. I think maybe this is the most literal use of ''black and white in colour'' that I''ve ever seen. heh.</td>', 'Too damned clever by half. More than half, judging by the voters'' reactions.An OOBIE nomination is a little oddball feather in your cap, even if your name isn''t pulled out of the envelope. You get my vote.Damn. I think maybe this is the most literal use of ''black and white in colour'' that I''ve ever seen. heh.', '2008-03-10 06:20:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553480, 651165, 64707, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by thedarkpose:</b></div><hr/><i> this is the ONLY image i have ever submitted on which i have not received any negative feedback :) .. happy me lol....<br/>and for those who could not relate to the title, id have a brief -<br/>when we are young, we are extremely playful, our whole existence is a play, keys becomes toys, and every tiny thing just becomes so much more playful... but as we grow older, and we learn about life, we lose that playfulness in ourselves, keys do nothing more than open doors.. so the balloons are symbolic to our childhood pleasures and "handicap" as we are no longer capable of getting any joy from them... lol i hope this makes sense ;) ..<br/> <br/>thanks to everyone who voted! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is the type of photography that inspired me to take it up - your explanation makes perfect sense to me.  Very nice.</td>', 'Originally posted by thedarkpose: this is the ONLY image i have ever submitted on which i have not received any negative feedback :) .. happy me lol....and for those who could not relate to the title, id have a brief -when we are young, we are extremely playful, our whole existence is a play, keys becomes toys, and every tiny thing just becomes so much more playful... but as we grow older, and we learn about life, we lose that playfulness in ourselves, keys do nothing more than open doors.. so the balloons are symbolic to our childhood pleasures and "handicap" as we are no longer capable of getting any joy from them... lol i hope this makes sense ;) .. thanks to everyone who voted!   This is the type of photography that inspired me to take it up - your explanation makes perfect sense to me.  Very nice.', '2008-03-10 21:47:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554040, 651419, 67579, '<td valign="top">Sweeeet! great pic and score :) <br/> <br/>Grats Jojo :)</td>', 'Sweeeet! great pic and score :)  Grats Jojo :)', '2008-03-11 00:57:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554542, 651736, 30049, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/><u>First Impression</u> <br/> <br/>Smile.  :-)  Simplicity.<br/> <br/><u>Looking Deeper</u> <br/> <br/>This photo met the challenge theme without question IMO.  That''s a feat in itself based on all the banter around what the challenge meant to different people.<br/> <br/>It''s very simple, and to the point.  The title, in combination, made me smile as I could visualize this poor leftover jelly bean getting left behind.  <br/> <br/>The simplicity gives the photo a feeling of a stock photo, especially with the white background.  Kind of static and impersonal.  I think this made the image an easy ''hit the 5'' and move on target during the challenge.  Nothing to hold the viewer''s interest for very long.<br/> <br/>From a technical standpoint I don''t see anything really out of place.  The focus is right on, lighting seems appropriate...if it was mine I''d have been tempted to clean up the few specks on the lower front of the jelly bean.  Small item, but some may have seen it as a lack of attention to detail.<br/> <br/>The new rules allow for image size up to 720px for advanced challenges now.  You only used 640...may have gotten a little more impact from the extra sizing.<br/> <br/>Had I been at your party, this jelly bean wouldn''t have survived; black is my favorite!  :-D<br/> <br/>Questions?  Please feel free to send me a PM.  Thanks!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club First Impression  Smile.  :-)  Simplicity. Looking Deeper  This photo met the challenge theme without question IMO.  That''s a feat in itself based on all the banter around what the challenge meant to different people. It''s very simple, and to the point.  The title, in combination, made me smile as I could visualize this poor leftover jelly bean getting left behind.   The simplicity gives the photo a feeling of a stock photo, especially with the white background.  Kind of static and impersonal.  I think this made the image an easy ''hit the 5'' and move on target during the challenge.  Nothing to hold the viewer''s interest for very long. From a technical standpoint I don''t see anything really out of place.  The focus is right on, lighting seems appropriate...if it was mine I''d have been tempted to clean up the few specks on the lower front of the jelly bean.  Small item, but some may have seen it as a lack of attention to detail. The new rules allow for image size up to 720px for advanced challenges now.  You only used 640...may have gotten a little more impact from the extra sizing. Had I been at your party, this jelly bean wouldn''t have survived; black is my favorite!  :-D Questions?  Please feel free to send me a PM.  Thanks!', '2008-03-11 09:12:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554571, 651162, 30049, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/><u>First Impression</u> <br/> <br/>Perfect!<br/> <br/><u>Looking Deeper</u> <br/> <br/>I love this photo.  It was my favorite from the challenge.  Your title says it all.  Simplicity!<br/> <br/>Compositionally, this is a piece of art.  For the challenge it''s a perfect fit.  Beauty in a stark, cold, yet serene setting.<br/> <br/>The diagonal of the layout is easy viewing and makes for a pleasant experience.  Granted, the image isn''t deep in concept so I don''t need to stay with it forever to take it all in.  The shadows help add depth and balance.  I see a hint of blue in the shadows, which makes sense and solidifies this in the challenge theme.<br/> <br/>Something that probably held this back a smidge is the jaggies from resizing on the tree trunks and shadows.  Hard to avoid, but still there nonetheless.  At full size (print) this probably isn''t an issue.<br/> <br/>Not sure what else to say.  Some probably could find some deeper philosophical meanings...me, I just like it.  :-D<br/> <br/>Job well done!<br/> <br/>Questions?  Please feel free to send me a PM.  Thanks!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club First Impression  Perfect! Looking Deeper  I love this photo.  It was my favorite from the challenge.  Your title says it all.  Simplicity! Compositionally, this is a piece of art.  For the challenge it''s a perfect fit.  Beauty in a stark, cold, yet serene setting. The diagonal of the layout is easy viewing and makes for a pleasant experience.  Granted, the image isn''t deep in concept so I don''t need to stay with it forever to take it all in.  The shadows help add depth and balance.  I see a hint of blue in the shadows, which makes sense and solidifies this in the challenge theme. Something that probably held this back a smidge is the jaggies from resizing on the tree trunks and shadows.  Hard to avoid, but still there nonetheless.  At full size (print) this probably isn''t an issue. Not sure what else to say.  Some probably could find some deeper philosophical meanings...me, I just like it.  :-D Job well done! Questions?  Please feel free to send me a PM.  Thanks!', '2008-03-11 09:25:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557232, 649288, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done - quite elegant in its simplicity!</td>', 'Very nicely done - quite elegant in its simplicity!', '2008-03-12 07:07:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557237, 652002, 30982, '<td valign="top">Can I just say "brrrrrrrr!"?  This is almost abstract in a way - very nice tones.  I''m amazed the water appears that black, too.  Neat shot!</td>', 'Can I just say "brrrrrrrr!"?  This is almost abstract in a way - very nice tones.  I''m amazed the water appears that black, too.  Neat shot!', '2008-03-12 07:08:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4557243, 650510, 30982, '<td valign="top">Haunting and mesmerizing at the same time.  A very good choice for this challenge.  (I was one of your "7s or higher" by the way.)</td>', 'Haunting and mesmerizing at the same time.  A very good choice for this challenge.  (I was one of your "7s or higher" by the way.)', '2008-03-12 07:09:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4558364, 652070, 67697, '<td valign="top">I bet if you did a crazy tilt, you''d get a sense that the tree was hanging on for dear life.  Hmmm this doesn''t look like you guys got much snow at all!  Actually, I think you would have also had a pretty shot without the concrete.  It looks pretty when the snow is clinging on to the branches like that.</td>', 'I bet if you did a crazy tilt, you''d get a sense that the tree was hanging on for dear life.  Hmmm this doesn''t look like you guys got much snow at all!  Actually, I think you would have also had a pretty shot without the concrete.  It looks pretty when the snow is clinging on to the branches like that.', '2008-03-12 14:28:16.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4561425, 651950, 90892, '<td valign="top">This is really nice pic. should have done better imo.</td>', 'This is really nice pic. should have done better imo.', '2008-03-13 11:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4565310, 651930, 69008, '<td valign="top">This B&amp;W in color challenge would be a rather tough one. I thought about entering it, but everything around here and out doors where I like to shoot has a lot of color in it.  <br/>This image is a good find, to get the light thru the pipes the way you did, and the shapes and lines are good too. I think that it got voted down in the challenge because there is a lot of noise in the darker areas, and, for this challenge, something with high contrast on very strong lines would have been better. <br/>The general low key (not bright) effect keeps the image from getting a lot of views from the thumbnail, because it is difficult to see what it is in thumbnail size.</td>', 'This B&W in color challenge would be a rather tough one. I thought about entering it, but everything around here and out doors where I like to shoot has a lot of color in it.  This image is a good find, to get the light thru the pipes the way you did, and the shapes and lines are good too. I think that it got voted down in the challenge because there is a lot of noise in the darker areas, and, for this challenge, something with high contrast on very strong lines would have been better. The general low key (not bright) effect keeps the image from getting a lot of views from the thumbnail, because it is difficult to see what it is in thumbnail size.', '2008-03-15 13:58:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566112, 650510, 60862, '<td valign="top">Charlene, I was one of your 4s.  I''m glad you found an appreciative audience in the folks who commented before me, though. :)<br/> <br/>I didn''t really get it, and I didn''t understand the blurred reflected figures.  I think the idea of capturing both the statues and the carvings is good, though.</td>', 'Charlene, I was one of your 4s.  I''m glad you found an appreciative audience in the folks who commented before me, though. :) I didn''t really get it, and I didn''t understand the blurred reflected figures.  I think the idea of capturing both the statues and the carvings is good, though.', '2008-03-15 20:17:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566113, 649288, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like this, Kelly. :)  My only suggestions would be to try to diffuse the light source so it doesn''t create a hot spot on the stone.</td>', 'I like this, Kelly. :)  My only suggestions would be to try to diffuse the light source so it doesn''t create a hot spot on the stone.', '2008-03-15 20:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566116, 652002, 60862, '<td valign="top">Ernie, the textures are nice, as Catherine said.  There''s just not much contrast to draw them out.</td>', 'Ernie, the textures are nice, as Catherine said.  There''s just not much contrast to draw them out.', '2008-03-15 20:20:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566119, 649660, 60862, '<td valign="top">As Catherine noted, it''s composed and lit nicely, but not much story to it.  I''d try brightening it, though - the background is probably white, but the current version is very gray.</td>', 'As Catherine noted, it''s composed and lit nicely, but not much story to it.  I''d try brightening it, though - the background is probably white, but the current version is very gray.', '2008-03-15 20:21:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566121, 650123, 60862, '<td valign="top">I liked this a lot, Jeb - gave you a 7.  The small amount of color didn''t bother me.</td>', 'I liked this a lot, Jeb - gave you a 7.  The small amount of color didn''t bother me.', '2008-03-15 20:22:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566124, 651962, 60862, '<td valign="top">Interesting composition, and I like how the water on the right seems to fall out of reality.</td>', 'Interesting composition, and I like how the water on the right seems to fall out of reality.', '2008-03-15 20:22:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566127, 651706, 60862, '<td valign="top">Classic shot of a classic subject, Terry. :)  Congrats on the great score!</td>', 'Classic shot of a classic subject, Terry. :)  Congrats on the great score!', '2008-03-15 20:23:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566131, 651807, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, Rob.  To improve it a bit, try two different crops:  one with most of the right side removed so the branch ends closer to the right edge and one much wider (if you have the pixels in the original).  Both would move the branch out of the middle.</td>', 'Nice shot, Rob.  To improve it a bit, try two different crops:  one with most of the right side removed so the branch ends closer to the right edge and one much wider (if you have the pixels in the original).  Both would move the branch out of the middle.', '2008-03-15 20:25:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566136, 649562, 60862, '<td valign="top">Steve, the idea is solid.  Try adding another light or two to the sides to soften the shadows.  Also try putting tissue over the flash or lamps (I use the kind you put in gift bags) to diffuse the light.<br/> <br/>Also, it''s worth learning the clone tool if your software supports it - the hairs on the bottom are distracting.</td>', 'Steve, the idea is solid.  Try adding another light or two to the sides to soften the shadows.  Also try putting tissue over the flash or lamps (I use the kind you put in gift bags) to diffuse the light. Also, it''s worth learning the clone tool if your software supports it - the hairs on the bottom are distracting.', '2008-03-15 20:27:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566141, 651979, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like it, Don.  I''m a sucker for nicely composed blurred bird shots.  Thanks for explaining about the signature - I agree with you.</td>', 'I like it, Don.  I''m a sucker for nicely composed blurred bird shots.  Thanks for explaining about the signature - I agree with you.', '2008-03-15 20:29:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4574113, 652059, 63398, '<td valign="top">Wow! I think that this image was horribly underrated! Terrific concept and execution! The cropping/composition to get the complete reflections is just superb!</td>', 'Wow! I think that this image was horribly underrated! Terrific concept and execution! The cropping/composition to get the complete reflections is just superb!', '2008-03-19 13:11:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4574728, 652018, 63267, '<td valign="top">Very nice photo Ryan.  Love the dropping ink.</td>', 'Very nice photo Ryan.  Love the dropping ink.', '2008-03-19 16:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
