(4694087, 651068, 41337, '<td valign="top">I hadn''t seen this before. What an image!</td>', 'I hadn''t seen this before. What an image!', '2008-05-10 16:57:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4720508, 651107, 63269, '<td valign="top">SUPERB lighting.</td>', 'SUPERB lighting.', '2008-05-23 20:26:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4760182, 651419, 63244, '<td valign="top">(Erm, so where did my original comment go?) I see a pink spot, lol!  HOw the heck did I miss this one.  It''s so creative...and so well lit!  Great job!  ~Now go wash the house paint off of your poor kiddos! :)</td>', '(Erm, so where did my original comment go?) I see a pink spot, lol!  HOw the heck did I miss this one.  It''s so creative...and so well lit!  Great job!  ~Now go wash the house paint off of your poor kiddos! :)', '2008-06-09 19:45:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4764177, 651973, 49804, '<td valign="top">Really nice shot, nailed the timing here, the one thing I would like to see would be added contrast, right now it looks rather flat, I think bringing up the contrast could add a lot of pop, here''s a quick edit I did, hope this is helpful, nonetheless, this is a really great shot.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=688018" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49804/120/688018.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49804/120/688018.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49804/120/688018.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I brought out some contrast in the splashing milk. I couldn''t get quite what I was thinking of, probably the best way to do it would be by bouncing the light off a wall to the side, it would add some contrast. Take it or leave it thought, just my opinion, really great shot still, keep it up.<br/> <br/>edit: changed the edit just a little.<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-11 13:43:50.</i></td>', 'Really nice shot, nailed the timing here, the one thing I would like to see would be added contrast, right now it looks rather flat, I think bringing up the contrast could add a lot of pop, here''s a quick edit I did, hope this is helpful, nonetheless, this is a really great shot.   I brought out some contrast in the splashing milk. I couldn''t get quite what I was thinking of, probably the best way to do it would be by bouncing the light off a wall to the side, it would add some contrast. Take it or leave it thought, just my opinion, really great shot still, keep it up. edit: changed the edit just a little. ', '2008-06-11 14:41:34.000000', '2008-06-11 14:43:50.000000', 0),
(4800924, 651419, 88136, '<td valign="top">WA!!! SOO cool! i seriously love this, fabulous job</td>', 'WA!!! SOO cool! i seriously love this, fabulous job', '2008-07-03 12:39:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4815595, 650426, 30807, '<td valign="top">Hmm..! Just slightly like the egg scene from Alien - makes my breakfast egg so much more scary than usual. Like the misty fog layer - just add a green laser layer, and your there<br/> <br/>You are very good at so many types of picture - just leafing through your shots. Keep going. I don''t know what work you do, but I would think you could do this full time - If you don''t run out of inspiration or zap!</td>', 'Hmm..! Just slightly like the egg scene from Alien - makes my breakfast egg so much more scary than usual. Like the misty fog layer - just add a green laser layer, and your there You are very good at so many types of picture - just leafing through your shots. Keep going. I don''t know what work you do, but I would think you could do this full time - If you don''t run out of inspiration or zap!', '2008-07-09 19:12:31.000000', NULL, 0),
